      ],
      "source": "https://grokipedia.com/page/nardin_oklahoma"
    },
    {
      "id": 2,
      "text": "Originally known as Vilott, the community was officially renamed Nardin on April 12, 1898.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        3,
        4
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Web source 1"
      ],
      "source": "https://grokipedia.com/page/nardin_oklahoma"
    },
    {
      "id": 3,
      "text": "The Atchison, Topeka and Santa Fe Railway once provided Nardin with a station to help transport agricultural goods.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        13,
